{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-116650-r4622764","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Nanaimo Bars I","sourcePageId":116650,"sourceRevision":"4622764","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-03-15T00:49:26Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Nanaimo%20Bars%20I&oldid=4622764","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:24.376Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Canadian recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes using almond","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cocoa powder","Category:Recipes using coconut","Category:Recipes using custard powder","Category:Recipes using dark chocolate","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using powdered sugar","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"b88983405e5b1df7bf7a5610f5c5508aa77b39a9b317261cfe7fb410e82e0ff3","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Recipes for dessert\n| Difficulty = 3\n| Image = [[File:Nanaimo bar.JPG|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Desserts]]\n\n'''Nanaimo Bars''' are a layered chocolate and [[Cookbook:Custard|custard]] dessert named after the mining town, Nanaimo, British Columbia, Canada. This winning recipe was submitted by Joyce Hardcastle in 1986 when the City of Nanaimo and Harbour Park Mall had a contest to find the best Nanaimo Bar recipe. Variations of this recipe include using different nuts and/or adding flavours to the custard layer.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== Bottom layer ===\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] unsalted [[Cookbook:butter|butter]] (European style cultured)\n* ¼ cup white granulated [[Cookbook:sugar|sugar]]\n* 5 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:cocoa|cocoa]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:egg|egg]] beaten\n* 1¼ cups [[Cookbook:Graham Cracker|graham wafer]] crumbs\n* ½ cups finely-[[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:almond|almonds]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:coconut|coconut]]\n\n=== Middle layer ===\n* ½ cup unsalted [[Cookbook:butter|butter]]\n* 2 tbsp and 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:cream|cream]]\n* 2 tbsp vanilla [[Cookbook:Custard Powder|custard powder]]\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Powdered Sugar|icing sugar]]\n\n=== Top layer ===\n* 4 squares (4 oz) semi-sweet [[Cookbook:chocolate|chocolate]]\n* 2 tbsp unsalted [[Cookbook:butter|butter]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n=== Bottom layer ===\n#Melt first 3 ingredients in top of [[Cookbook:Double Boiler|double boiler]].\n#Add egg and stir to cook and thicken.\n#Remove from heat. Stir in crumbs, coconut, and nuts.\n#Press firmly into an ungreased 8 x 8-inch [[Cookbook:Cake Pan|cake pan]].\n\n=== Middle layer ===\n#[[Cookbook:Creaming|Cream]] butter, cream, custard powder, and icing sugar together well. [[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] until light. \n#Spread over bottom layer.\n\n=== Top layer ===\n#Melt chocolate and butter over low heat. Cool. \n#Once cool, but still liquid, pour over second layer and chill in refrigerator.\n#Once set, cut into squares and serve. Enjoy.\n\n[[Category:Canadian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using almond]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using powdered sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dark chocolate]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cocoa powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coconut]]\n[[Category:Recipes using custard powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Nanaimo Bars I","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ cup unsalted butter (European style cultured)","sourceText":"½ cup unsalted butter (European style cultured)","amountText":"½ cup unsalted butter (European style cultured)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"¼ cup white granulated sugar","sourceText":"¼ cup white granulated sugar","amountText":"¼ cup white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"5 tbsp cocoa","sourceText":"5 tbsp cocoa","amountText":"5 tbsp cocoa","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 egg beaten","sourceText":"1 egg beaten","amountText":"1 egg beaten","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1¼ cups graham wafer crumbs","sourceText":"1¼ cups graham wafer crumbs","amountText":"1¼ cups graham wafer crumbs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"½ cups finely-chopped almonds","sourceText":"½ cups finely-chopped almonds","amountText":"½ cups finely-chopped almonds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 cup coconut","sourceText":"1 cup coconut","amountText":"1 cup coconut","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"½ cup unsalted butter","sourceText":"½ cup unsalted butter","amountText":"½ cup unsalted butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"2 tbsp and 2 tsp cream","sourceText":"2 tbsp and 2 tsp cream","amountText":"2 tbsp and 2 tsp cream","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"2 tbsp vanilla custard powder","sourceText":"2 tbsp vanilla custard powder","amountText":"2 tbsp vanilla custard powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-11","name":"2 cups icing sugar","sourceText":"2 cups icing sugar","amountText":"2 cups icing sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-12","name":"4 squares (4 oz) semi-sweet chocolate","sourceText":"4 squares (4 oz) semi-sweet chocolate","amountText":"4 squares (4 oz) semi-sweet chocolate","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-13","name":"2 tbsp unsalted butter","sourceText":"2 tbsp unsalted butter","amountText":"2 tbsp unsalted butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Melt first 3 ingredients in top of double boiler.","sourceText":"Melt first 3 ingredients in top of double boiler.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Add egg and stir to cook and thicken.","sourceText":"Add egg and stir to cook and thicken.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Remove from heat. Stir in crumbs, coconut, and nuts.","sourceText":"Remove from heat. Stir in crumbs, coconut, and nuts.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Press firmly into an ungreased 8 x 8-inch cake pan.","sourceText":"Press firmly into an ungreased 8 x 8-inch cake pan.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Cream butter, cream, custard powder, and icing sugar together well. Beat until light.","sourceText":"Cream butter, cream, custard powder, and icing sugar together well. Beat until light.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Spread over bottom layer.","sourceText":"Spread over bottom layer.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":7,"text":"Melt chocolate and butter over low heat. Cool.","sourceText":"Melt chocolate and butter over low heat. Cool.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":8,"text":"Once cool, but still liquid, pour over second layer and chill in refrigerato